// Overriding an inherited non-async function with an async one must be
// rejected. The base program is already compiled, and the call inside its
// use() was typed against `int f()`. Were this allowed, that call would
// receive a promise instead: `if (f(1))` becomes unconditionally true and the
// first arithmetic on the result errors at runtime, far from the cause.
// Changing any other part of the return type across an override already
// warns; this one has no runtime check behind it at all, so it is an error.
inherit "/clone/async_override_base";

async int f(int n) {
  return n + 100;
}
